WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.290
Did you know that there are two Pirates of
the Caribbean scripts currently in development?

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:09.550
So, could Jack Sparrow fans see Johnny Depp
reprise his iconic role, now that his defamation

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.420
trial against ex-wife Amber Heard is over?

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.490
The answer may surprise you.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.199
Finally, after more than a month of deliberation,
the jury hearing Johnny Depp and Amber Heard's

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:22.439
competing defamation lawsuits has reached
a verdict.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:27.980
To briefly recap, Heard and Depp were married
from 2015 to 2017, and Heard alleges that

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.579
Depp was abusive to her during this time.

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:36.211
In 2018, Heard identified herself as a "public
figure representing domestic abuse" in an

00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:38.450
essay for The Washington Post.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.690
Depp characterized the allegations as a hoax
and claimed that Heard had been the one abusing

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.690
him.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.710
"I can't say that I'm embarrassed because
I know that I'm doing the right thing."

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.270
Depp then claimed that the allegation caused
him to lose out on lucrative acting roles.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:01:00.030
In late 2018, Depp sued Heard in Virginia
for defamation, seeking $50 million in damages.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.210
The impact on Depp's career is central to
his lawsuit.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:07.320
Under questioning from his own lawyer, Depp
claimed that Disney dropped him from the Pirates

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.210
of the Caribbean franchise after Heard's essay
was published.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.009
Heard responded with a countersuit over Depp's
hoax allegations, claiming that Depp orchestrated

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:21.540
a campaign to get her fired from Aquaman and
from her job as a L'oréal spokesperson.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:27.039
Depp already lost a similar defamation lawsuit
in the United Kingdom in November 2020, and

00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:29.810
an appeal over that decision the following
March.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:36.789
However, on June 1, 2022, the American jury
sided with Depp on all three counts of defamation,

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:41.220
awarding him $15 million in compensatory and
punitive damages.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.029
The jury also upheld one of Heard's claims
of defamation, awarding her $2 million in

00:01:46.029 --> 00:01:47.820
compensatory damages.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.170
Now that the verdict is in, here's how it
could affect Depp's role in the Pirates of

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.979
the Caribbean franchise going forward.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.539
"Captain, captain Jack Sparrow."

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:00.719
Currently, there are two Pirates of the Caribbean
scripts in development, which would make the

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:03.630
sixth and seventh installments in the franchise.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:08.009
Producer Jerry Bruckheimer spoke about Johnny
Depp's future as Jack Sparrow weeks before

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:09.890
the verdict was reached.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:13.810
When asked if Disney was planning to cast
Depp in the sixth film, Bruckheimer responded,

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.110
"Not at this point."

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.420
As it turns out, though, there might not be
a need for Depp in Pirates of the Caribbean

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.840
6 anyway.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.540
Bruckheimer also revealed that the script
is centered on a female lead, with Margot

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.790
Robbie in mind.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.770
That would seem to eliminate the need for
Jack Sparrow to factor into the story.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:33.950
On the other hand, the seventh film isn't
centered around Robbie's possible character,

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.780
which could leave room for Jack Sparrow to
return in some capacity.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.050
Bruckheimer added that "the future is yet
to be decided."

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.570
So, Bruckheimer was already leaving the door
open for a possible Depp return before the

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.440
verdict was reached.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.160
Script specifics aside, the biggest question
is whether Disney wants to work with Depp

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.730
again or not.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.640
The trial has undoubtedly tarnished Depp's
reputation.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.970
Still, Bruckheimer's comments don't explicitly
rule out Depp's potential return.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:03.620
Therefore, there's no guarantee Depp will
ever play Jack Sparrow again, but it sounds

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.040
like it hasn't been ruled out.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.920
At the same time, it's important to consider
that Disney is only half of the equation.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.600
Johnny Depp may not even want to come back
as Jack Sparrow after all that he's gone through

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.830
and how his relationship with the Walt Disney
Company has shifted in recent years.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.320
In fact, during the trial, Depp confirmed
previous testimony that his connection with

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.470
the company has changed so drastically that
he wouldn't return to the role no matter how

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.910
much Disney offered.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.450
"Nothing on this earth would get you to go
back and work with Disney on a 'Pirates of

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.460
the Caribbean' film.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.460
Correct?"

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.830
"That is true Mr. Rottenborn."

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.070
The actor explained during his trial testimony:

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.300
"There was a deep and distinct sense of feeling
betrayed by the people that I've worked hard

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.310
for.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:47.330
People that I delivered a character to that
they initially despised, but I stuck to my

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.280
guns with the character, and it seemed to
work."

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.070
While this could be pure hyperbole, considering
the circumstances, Depp's likely serious for

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.250
the time being.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.870
Time will tell when the next Pirates of the
Caribbean project will sail into theaters,

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.020
but as things stand at the time of the Johnny
Depp-Amber Heard verdict, don't expect to

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.130
see Captain Jack Sparrow back in action when
it does.

